# Architectural Bakery Facade and Illuminated Wooden Sign

Status: DONE
Milestone: M34 A complete grounded illustrated shopfront
Dependencies: 36_PAINTERLY_WINDOWLIT_INTERIOR.todo; 37_HANGING_DOOR_OPEN_SIGN.todo

## Purpose

The owner rejects the entrance as a floating sign, canopy and oversized doors.
They want a believable complete bakery building in a warm hand-painted animation
direction, with the wooden board and raised glowing identity already used on the
main header. References provide architectural inspiration only.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve the completed b74acc7 release and all current local authoring work.
- [x] Record the architectural direction and assign the facade implementation.
- [x] Build a coherent roof/upper-storey, sign fascia, supported canopy and framed shopfront.
- [x] Add a grounded plinth/threshold/pavement and restrained original planting/details.
- [x] Use the original wood texture, mark and Courgette wordmark with warm raised lighting.
- [x] Keep a single coherent interior behind glazing and door-local OPEN plaque.
- [x] Fit desktop, portrait mobile and short screens without clipping controls or signage.
- [x] Preserve click/keyboard entry, bell, skip, look-around and complete resource fallbacks.
- [x] Review source, actual pixels/geometry, lighting, readability and viewport behavior.
- [x] Refresh affected launch artwork and documentation, then publish scoped output.

## Acceptance criteria

- The entrance has a complete building silhouette, not disconnected floating UI shapes.
- Cornices, columns, window recesses, awning, base and pavement have consistent support/depth.
- Continuous wooden entrance fascia and static raised/backlit original identity are readable.
- Original cream/deep-green/terracotta/blush accents; no global site palette change.
- No copied reference pixels, stock watermarks, signs, characters or exact composition.
- Interior camera, real media, notebooks, main header and page fabric behavior are preserved.
- No questions, new image-tool views or unearned aesthetic/perfection claims.

